# CASP15 T1170 — The DNA Repair Machine (7PBR)
---

This is RuvB — a molecular motor that repairs
damaged DNA.

Published in Nature in 2022 by Wald and colleagues,
this structure revealed how cells fix one of the
most dangerous types of DNA damage.

> close
> load 7pbr
---

RuvB forms a hexameric ring — six copies of the
same protein arranged in a circle.

This ring wraps around DNA and uses the energy
from ATP to drive branch migration of
Holliday junctions — the crossover points
that form when chromosomes recombine.

> spin 0.15
---

Let's look at the fuel that powers this machine.

Each subunit binds ATP or ADP, and the coordinated
hydrolysis around the ring creates a rotary motor
that physically pushes DNA through the complex.

> stop
> view ligand
---

Without RuvB, cells cannot properly repair
double-strand breaks in DNA — the most lethal
form of DNA damage.

Understanding this machine helps us understand
both cancer and the DNA repair pathways
that protect us from it.

> reset
> spin 0.1
---

RuvB helicase — the molecular motor that
saves your genome.
PDB code 7PBR, CASP15 target T1170.

> stop
